 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Not quite. It's 10 miles, which is long ride for most people. Roughly few hours, depending on your speed. Would you do it in one go, or stop and rest along the way? It is, and it a good way to see the countryside too. If you stop, you could return the same day, or stay overnight. Start at sunset and you still have light for the descent. You see more too, even on quiet road. Start with shorter rides and build up, maybe mix in some hills. A week or two of regular riding will make you confident.",
